From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:53:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] screenshot: Copy each eye into the stereo picture as it
 is

A stereo capture renders each eye into the frame and joins the two
pictures side by side in a new QImage, which was not filled, with
QPainter's default composition, source over. Where an eye is transparent
(nothing covers the output there, and the frame is cleared to
transparent black), the joined picture kept whatever the new image's
memory held: a capture taken after an earlier one showed leftovers of
freed pictures in the columns Stereo KWin cuts from a wallpaper's sides.

The eyes are now copied with CompositionMode_Source, transparent pixels
included, so the joined picture holds exactly what was rendered.

testUncoveredPixelsAreTransparentInBothEyes fills and frees pictures of
the joined picture's size before each of three captures of a stereo
output with one small window, and checks that every pixel no window
covers is transparent black in both eyes; without the change the first
capture already shows the freed memory.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
